    "https://wheatoncollege.edu/academics/life-and-career-design-institute/employers/": {
      "title": "Employers",
      "description": "Employers - Wheaton College Massachusetts Skip to main content Skip to main content Navigation menu Alumni Athletics Giving Parents & Families insideWheaton Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Academics Academics Academic Calendar Accreditation Academic Advising College Catalog Departments Faculty Directory Global Education Library Life and Career Design Institute Programs Projects & Initiatives Provost Summer Session The Wheaton Curriculum Winter Session Admission Admission Admitted Students Applying to Wheaton Scholarships Information for Counselors International Students Meet the Admission Staff Picture #WheatonMA Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Visiting Wheaton Campus Life Campus Life Athletics and Recreation Clubs & Organizations Dean of Students First Year Resources Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Marshall Center Safety on Campus Wheaton Orientation Programs About Wheaton About Wheaton Campus & Community Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging History & Traditions Honor Code Mission and Vision Offices & Services Outcomes & Impact President & College Leadership Sustainability Facts and Figures The Wheaton Edge Working at Wheaton Search What can we help you find? type keywords here Search Visit Wheaton Learn about how and when you can visit our campus Request Info Receive announcements and materials based upon your academic interests. Apply Now Ready to apply? Check out our requirements and deadlines. × Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Employers Life and Career Design Institute Home » Academics » Life and Career Design Institute » Employers Our relationship with employers is important to us and we want our students to have every opportunity to connect with you! Hire a Lyon! Recruit Wheaton’s talented students and alumni Post part-time internships and jobs for current students and full-time positions for graduating seniors and alumni in Handshake. Create an account as an employer and request approval to post positions. New employer requests are reviewed daily. Recruit at Wheaton Posting positions on Handshake allows you to have the broadest reach possible and it ensures all job postings are accessible to all students . If your organization regularly recruits at colleges, you may have a Handshake account already. Here are some other resources you might find helpful. Getting started with Handshake as an employer Create an employer user account, join a company and connect with schools (Wheaton College MA) How to create a new employer profile How to post a job Your end-to-end virtual recruiting strategy Employer Events Wheaton College is a liberal arts college offering 100 academic programs to 1,700 undergraduate students and 23,000 alumni. We welcome organizations interested in recruiting for internships, part-time work, or full-time opportunities. Contact the Life and Career Design Institute at [email protected] for more information. Spring Career Fair Hundreds of students meet with employers from the New England area at Wheaton’s Spring Career Fair to learn about job and internship opportunities and participate in on-campus interviews. On-Campus Information Sessions Reserve a classroom or an information table to educate students about your organization. Sessions can be scheduled anytime during the year. On-Campus Interviews Schedule time to interview students for opportunities within your organization. Request an interview schedule on Handshake . Wheaton College adheres to the U.S. Department of Labor guidelines (.pdf) and the National Association of Colleges and Employers Best Practices to define internship experiences. Employers considering creating and/or posting internship positions should meet these guidelines. NOTE: Wheaton College does not enter into affiliation agreements with employers on behalf of individual student interns. Scroll to Top Wheaton College - Massachusetts 26 E. Main Street Norton, MA 02766 508-286-8200 Arts Directions Map News Blog Magazine Academic Calendar Events Calendar Bookstore Emergency Information Working at Wheaton Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Facebook LinkedIN Instagram TikTok YouTube © 2026 Wheaton College (MA) Accessibility Consumer Disclosures Contact Wheaton Policies Privacy Policy Title IX Website Feedback"
    },
    "https://wheatoncollege.edu/alumni/alumni-career-resources/": {
      "title": "Alumni Career Resources",
      "description": "Alumni Career Resources - Wheaton College Massachusetts Skip to main content Skip to main content Navigation menu Alumni Athletics Giving Parents & Families insideWheaton Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Academics Academics Academic Calendar Accreditation Academic Advising College Catalog Departments Faculty Directory Global Education Library Life and Career Design Institute Programs Projects & Initiatives Provost Summer Session The Wheaton Curriculum Winter Session Admission Admission Admitted Students Applying to Wheaton Scholarships Information for Counselors International Students Meet the Admission Staff Picture #WheatonMA Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Visiting Wheaton Campus Life Campus Life Athletics and Recreation Clubs & Organizations Dean of Students First Year Resources Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Marshall Center Safety on Campus Wheaton Orientation Programs About Wheaton About Wheaton Campus & Community Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging History & Traditions Honor Code Mission and Vision Offices & Services Outcomes & Impact President & College Leadership Sustainability Facts and Figures The Wheaton Edge Working at Wheaton Search What can we help you find? type keywords here Search Visit Wheaton Learn about how and when you can visit our campus Request Info Receive announcements and materials based upon your academic interests. Apply Now Ready to apply? Check out our requirements and deadlines. × Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Alumni Career Resources Home » Alumni » Alumni Career Resources More in this section Alumni Career Resources Alumni Authors Alumni Authors Form Alumni Podcasts Alumni Podcasts Form Alumni-Owned Small Business Form Alumni-Owned Small Businesses You started your career exploration at Wheaton. Now, we’re here to support you throughout your professional journey. Our alumni career resources help you connect with the Wheaton community to support your career goals—whether you are just starting out, want to advance in your field, or try something new. Career Resources Wheaton offers a number of alumni career resources to help you grow your professional network and connect with fellow alumni across industries. Young Alumni Handshake Sign up for Handshake and set Wheaton College as your affiliated school. Once you set up your profile and customize your preferences, you’ll receive a curated list of internships and jobs that match your skills and interests. You also can connect with other alumni on the platform and engage with employers. All Alumni Life and Career Design Institute Whether you’re just starting out or looking to take your next step, we’ll help you level up your career and professional skills. Schedule an appointment with the Life and Career Design Institute to explore career options, learn about job opportunities, get feedback on your resume, hone your interview skills or learn salary negotiation strategies. LinkedIn Check out our Wheaton College (MA) Alumni LinkedIn page to follow the career paths of fellow Wheaties. You can connect with alumni who work in your field or at a company you’re interested in exploring. It’s also a great way to engage in professional conversation and share successes, resources and job openings. Inspire and Hire Recent graduates and seasoned professionals have many opportunities to inspire current students. If you’re interested in speaking on a career panel, leading a professional development workshop, hosting a webinar, or mentoring a student, contact Wheaton’s Life and Career Design Institute at [email protected] . Plus, use our career networking platforms to recruit fellow alumni. With one click you can connect with up-and-coming talent, mid-career professionals and C-suite executives. Create an employer account on Handshake or post jobs and internships on our Alumni LinkedIn page . Alumni Businesses and Creative Works Our alumni community is full of creative entrepreneurs who share their passion and talents. Check out the links below to see how you can support them or have your creative work or small business featured on our site. Alumni Authors Alumni Podcasts Alumni Owned Small Businesses Diploma and Transcript Requests Whether you’re applying to graduate school, need to provide proof of education to your employer, or lost your diploma, send us a diploma or transcript request and we’ll send you an official copy for your records. Diploma and Transcript Requests Let’s Get Social Follow us on social to see what’s happening on campus and share your Wheaton pride with your followers. Keep in Touch We send lots of news via email. Send us your updated contact information so you don’t miss out on exciting announcements. Update Your Contact Information Questions? To contact the Alumni Relations Office , please email [email protected] or call 508-286-8207 . Scroll to Top Wheaton College - Massachusetts 26 E. Main Street Norton, MA 02766 508-286-8200 Arts Directions Map News Blog Magazine Academic Calendar Events Calendar Bookstore Emergency Information Working at Wheaton Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Facebook LinkedIN Instagram TikTok YouTube © 2026 Wheaton College (MA) Accessibility Consumer Disclosures Contact Wheaton Policies Privacy Policy Title IX Website Feedback"
    },
    "https://wheatoncollege.edu/academics/life-and-career-design-institute/parents/": {
      "title": "Parents",
      "description": "Parents - Wheaton College Massachusetts Skip to main content Skip to main content Navigation menu Alumni Athletics Giving Parents & Families insideWheaton Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Academics Academics Academic Calendar Accreditation Academic Advising College Catalog Departments Faculty Directory Global Education Library Life and Career Design Institute Programs Projects & Initiatives Provost Summer Session The Wheaton Curriculum Winter Session Admission Admission Admitted Students Applying to Wheaton Scholarships Information for Counselors International Students Meet the Admission Staff Picture #WheatonMA Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Visiting Wheaton Campus Life Campus Life Athletics and Recreation Clubs & Organizations Dean of Students First Year Resources Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Marshall Center Safety on Campus Wheaton Orientation Programs About Wheaton About Wheaton Campus & Community Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging History & Traditions Honor Code Mission and Vision Offices & Services Outcomes & Impact President & College Leadership Sustainability Facts and Figures The Wheaton Edge Working at Wheaton Search What can we help you find? type keywords here Search Visit Wheaton Learn about how and when you can visit our campus Request Info Receive announcements and materials based upon your academic interests. Apply Now Ready to apply? Check out our requirements and deadlines. × Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Parents Life and Career Design Institute Home » Academics » Life and Career Design Institute » Parents Accessibility notice: This page includes links to external websites that are not maintained by Wheaton College. External sites may not meet the same accessibility standards as our website. If you experience difficulty accessing information on an external site, please contact us at [email protected] . Career exploration is an ongoing process and it’s not unusual for students to have multiple interests or to feel confused at times about academic and career choices. Students who engage with Career Services early and often graduate with more confidence in their career decisions. Encourage your student to visit Career Services in their first semester and get on track to make the most of their four years. Partner with Us Join our network of professionals committed to providing students with relevant industry information. Fill out a volunteer form today. Participate in professional development programs on campus Speak on major and career-related panels Fill out an engagement request form today (Google Form)* * Note: We want to ensure our forms are accessible to everyone. If you have difficulty using this Google Form or require an alternative format, please contact us at [email protected] . Hire a Lyon! Post a job or internship. Create an account as an employer and request approval to post positions through Handshake. New employer requests are reviewed daily. Recruit at Wheaton Posting positions on Handshake allows you to have the broadest reach possible and it ensures all job postings are accessible to all students. If your organization regularly recruits at colleges, you may have a Handshake account already. Here are some other resources you might find helpful. Getting started with Handshake as an employer Create an employer user account, join a company and connect with schools (Wheaton College MA) How to create a new employer profile How to post a job Your end-to-end virtual recruiting strategy Wheaton College adheres to the U.S. Department of Labor guidelines (.PDF) , and the National Association of Colleges and Employers Best Practices to define internship experiences.  Employers considering creating and/or posting internship positions should meet these guidelines. Scroll to Top Wheaton College - Massachusetts 26 E. Main Street Norton, MA 02766 508-286-8200 Arts Directions Map News Blog Magazine Academic Calendar Events Calendar Bookstore Emergency Information Working at Wheaton Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Facebook LinkedIN Instagram TikTok YouTube © 2026 Wheaton College (MA) Accessibility Consumer Disclosures Contact Wheaton Policies Privacy Policy Title IX Website Feedback"
    },
    "https://wheatoncollege.edu/academics/life-and-career-design-institute/faculty/": {
      "title": "Faculty",
      "description": "Faculty - Wheaton College Massachusetts Skip to main content Skip to main content Navigation menu Alumni Athletics Giving Parents & Families insideWheaton Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Academics Academics Academic Calendar Accreditation Academic Advising College Catalog Departments Faculty Directory Global Education Library Life and Career Design Institute Programs Projects & Initiatives Provost Summer Session The Wheaton Curriculum Winter Session Admission Admission Admitted Students Applying to Wheaton Scholarships Information for Counselors International Students Meet the Admission Staff Picture #WheatonMA Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Visiting Wheaton Campus Life Campus Life Athletics and Recreation Clubs & Organizations Dean of Students First Year Resources Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Marshall Center Safety on Campus Wheaton Orientation Programs About Wheaton About Wheaton Campus & Community Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging History & Traditions Honor Code Mission and Vision Offices & Services Outcomes & Impact President & College Leadership Sustainability Facts and Figures The Wheaton Edge Working at Wheaton Search What can we help you find? type keywords here Search Visit Wheaton Learn about how and when you can visit our campus Request Info Receive announcements and materials based upon your academic interests. Apply Now Ready to apply? Check out our requirements and deadlines. × Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Faculty Life and Career Design Institute Home » Academics » Life and Career Design Institute » Faculty The Life and Career Design Institute offers many opportunities for faculty to support the connections between the classroom and careers. Whether you’d like to discuss career programs and workshops customized to a specific course or enhance the experiential learning opportunities for your students, we’re here to help. Partner with us by: Helping students be resourceful with their Wheaton funding. Use the Funding Opportunities page as a resource Adding NACE (National Association of Colleges and Employers) career competencies on your syllabus and/or learning outcomes for students Encouraging students to activate their free Handshake account If you are a club advisor, consider collaborating with a career advisor Request a career workshop for your class Please encourage your students to schedule an appointment with the Life and Career Design Institute . We can help them identify interests and skills, explore career paths, reflect on connections between academic and professional interests, and prepare for employment and/or graduate school after Wheaton. What We Offer First-Year Seminars We provide first-year students with an introduction to the Life and Career Design Institute. Then, we help them explore internships that connect their seminar with other out-of-class learning opportunities. Workshops Faculty can request workshops focused on: creating resumes, writing cover letters, interviewing, presentation skills, job and internship searches for various disciplines, professional etiquette or customized topics at your request. Senior Seminar Visits Students are encouraged to invite staff to their Senior Seminar (preferably before spring break). Staff can speak about resumes, networking, transitioning from Wheaton to the post-graduation world and more. Departmental Visits We are available to discuss the department-specific career exploration needs of your students. We can also partner to create discipline specific web content, highlighting internships for current students and the successes of Wheaton graduates. Resources for faculty What Can I Do With This Major? This resource provides an opportunity for students to understand potential career paths across a variety of majors and industries, identify actions they can take to progress professionally in those industries and access resources specific to those career paths. What Can I Do With This Major? Handshake Handshake allows students to search for jobs and internships in addition to providing a wide range of career resources. Handshake GoinGlobal This resource offers students access to worldwide job and internship opportunities as well as country-specific employment resources, including salary information, cost-of-living calculations, and employment trends in more than 80 countries GoinGlobal Connect with Us Hours: Monday–Friday, 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m. Location: Kollett Hall [email protected] Make an appointment Meet our team Scroll to Top Wheaton College - Massachusetts 26 E. Main Street Norton, MA 02766 508-286-8200 Arts Directions Map News Blog Magazine Academic Calendar Events Calendar Bookstore Emergency Information Working at Wheaton Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Facebook LinkedIN Instagram TikTok YouTube © 2026 Wheaton College (MA) Accessibility Consumer Disclosures Contact Wheaton Policies Privacy Policy Title IX Website Feedback"
    },
    "https://wheatoncollege.edu/academics/life-and-career-design-institute/meet-the-staff/": {
      "title": "Meet the Staff",
      "description": "Meet the Staff - LCDI - Wheaton College Massachusetts Skip to main content Skip to main content Navigation menu Alumni Athletics Giving Parents & Families insideWheaton Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Academics Academics Academic Calendar Accreditation Academic Advising College Catalog Departments Faculty Directory Global Education Library Life and Career Design Institute Programs Projects & Initiatives Provost Summer Session The Wheaton Curriculum Winter Session Admission Admission Admitted Students Applying to Wheaton Scholarships Information for Counselors International Students Meet the Admission Staff Picture #WheatonMA Transfer Students Tuition & Fees Visiting Wheaton Campus Life Campus Life Athletics and Recreation Clubs & Organizations Dean of Students First Year Resources Health & Wellness Housing & Dining Marshall Center Safety on Campus Wheaton Orientation Programs About Wheaton About Wheaton Campus & Community Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging History & Traditions Honor Code Mission and Vision Offices & Services Outcomes & Impact President & College Leadership Sustainability Facts and Figures The Wheaton Edge Working at Wheaton Search What can we help you find? type keywords here Search Visit Wheaton Learn about how and when you can visit our campus Request Info Receive announcements and materials based upon your academic interests. Apply Now Ready to apply? Check out our requirements and deadlines. × Visit Get Info Apply Give Now Meet the Staff Life and Career Design Institute Home » Academics » Life and Career Design Institute » Meet the Staff More in this section Meet the Staff Career Peer Advisors Formerly Career Services, the Life and Career Design Institute team can help you design your path to professional success. Our team is made up of professionals who have experience helping students to achieve their professional goals. Kathleen Potter, M.B.A. Director, Life and Career Navigation [email protected] Kelsey Pickering Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Engagement [email protected] Karen Single Career Navigator [email protected] Pronouns: she, her, hers Office Hours Hours: Monday–Friday, 8:30 a.m.–4:30 p.m. Location: Kollett Hall [email protected] Career Peer Advisors In addition to 1:1 advising, they work to gather resources and interview professionals in their career communities to gain hands-on insight and knowledge in the field(s). Additionally, career peer advisors receive intensive weekly training and professional development throughout the semester to best serve students. Career peer advisors can advise students from any class year; however, they meet with first and second-year students prior to their first meeting with one of our full-time career advisors in order to help them make the most out of their appointment. They also respond to inquiries and review resumes using the [email protected] email address. Meet with a Career Peer Advisor in the Career Design Studio (Kollett Hall) Our team of career peer advisors is available to assist with a variety of career-related topics, such as resumes, cover letters, utilizing Handshake and LinkedIn and more. Drop in to meet with a trained career peer advisor to help with career basics in the new Filene Center for Academic Advising and Career Services. Career Peer Advisor Drop-in Fall 2025 Hours Monday – Thursday: 2:00 – 9:00 p.m. Friday: 10:00 a.m. – 12:00 p.m. Scroll to Top Wheaton College - Massachusetts 26 E. Main Street Norton, MA 02766 508-286-8200 Arts Directions Map News Blog Magazine Academic Calendar Events Calendar Bookstore Emergency Information Working at Wheaton Diversity, Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Facebook LinkedIN Instagram TikTok YouTube © 2026 Wheaton College (MA) Accessibility Consumer Disclosures Contact Wheaton Policies Privacy Policy Title IX Website Feedback"
    },
