M experience preferred.High school diploma or equivalent required.Preferred ExperienceMerchant Cash Advance (MCA)Business LendingSBA LoansEquipment FinancingCommercial LendingBusiness DevelopmentFinancial SalesInside SalesBusiness BankingCompensation & BenefitsUncapped commission structurePerformance bonuses and incentivesQualified inbound leads availableOngoing sales and product trainingOpportunities for career advancementSupportive and collaborative team environmentFlexible work schedule (where applicable)Ideal CandidateYou are a motivated sales professional who enjoys helping business owners succeed. You are comfortable speaking with decision-makers, handling objections, and closing deals. You thrive in a competitive environment and are driven by unlimited earning potential.If you're looking to build a rewarding career in commercial finance with a growing organization, we'd love to hear from you. Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:36:14 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11289437/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11289872 Associate Contracts Administrator at Kitware Employer: Kitware \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n Kitware's Contracts team collaborates with our technical, finance, and business development teams to submit quality proposals for project funding opportunities and negotiates contracts with a wide variety of customers, subcontractors, and vendors. We pride ourselves on our ability to provide superior service and expertise that contributes to the company’s mission to solve complex problems and deliver innovative software solutions to our customers.Kitware seeks an Associate Contracts Administrator to assist with all aspects of the contracting lifecycle for government and industry customers. The administrator will be responsible for assisting in the preparation of proposals and the administration of contracts,  as well as providing post-award support.The Associate Contracts Administrator will interact with project managers, team members, auditors, collaborators, customers, and vendors in various capacities. Kitware’s customers range from startups to Fortune 500 companies, government agencies, and academic laboratories worldwide.In This Position You Will:Assist with preparation of proposals in response to solicitationsInterface with subcontractors to obtain necessary data for proposals, including pricing informationPrepare and disseminate proper instructions to the internal organization on contract requirementsAssist with the monitoring of projects to ensure all contract actions are being processed in a timely manner Administer contract modificationsComplete post-award administrative reporting requirementsMaintain close contact with customers and collaborators, fostering long-term business relationshipsAct as a point of contact for external organizations and internal individuals for proposal and contract related activitiesMaintain documents and input data into Kitware’s contract management systemPerform such other assignments as may be required from time to time by managementRequired Qualifications:Minimum of a bachelor's degree (preferably in humanities, business, or something similar)Strong communication, text analysis, and research skillsComputer literate in Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint) and an ability to learn Kitware’s internal systemsStrong organizational skills and ability to multitask and prioritizeAbility to work both independently and collaborativelyAbility and willingness to work in the office a minimum of three days per weekDue to contractual requirements, only US citizens will be considered for this positionPreferred Qualifications:Experience with Google Docs Familiarity with contracting principles and legal terms and conditionsOne year of demonstrated experience working in a professional environment Mon, 10 Aug 2026 17:44:59 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11289872/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11196883 Technical Sales Engineer at Balluff Inc Employer: Balluff Inc \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n Launch Your Career in Technical Sales with BalluffCalling December 2026 grads in engineering, business, or technical fields — this is your chance to step into a career in automation sales with a global industry leader. Balluff is expanding, and we're looking for future sales professionals to join our Sales Trainee Engagement Program (STEP).This 12-month, paid rotational training program will prepare you to become a Technical Sales Engineer within a defined sales territory at Balluff. You'll gain hands-on experience across key departments, build product knowledge, and learn how to deliver customer-focused solutions in industrial automation.What You'll ExperienceDuring the STEP program, you will:· Rotate through Balluff’s core functions: Technical Customer Support, Sales Support, Operations, and more· Learn how our products work by solving real customer applications and building solutions· Participate in structured product and sales training programs· Gain experience with internal systems, customer communication, and demo tools· Travel with and shadow experienced Sales Engineers· Begin building customer relationships via virtual sales activitiesWhat Makes You a Great FitWe're looking for curious, driven individuals who:· Enjoy solving problems and improving efficiency· Are naturally curious about how things work· Manage time well and are goal-oriented· Work well independently and as part of a team· Communicate confidently and clearly· Are eager to keep learning every dayWhy Join Balluff?· Competitive base salary + incentive program· Paid relocation support· Comprehensive benefits (medical, dental, vision, 401(k) with match)· Paid time off and holidays· Career growth and mentorship from experienced sales professionals· Be part of a high-growth global company with a strong commitment to innovationBasic Requirements· Bachelor’s degree in engineering, business, or a technical discipline· Up to 1–2 years of post-education experience· Technical aptitude with a willingness to learn Balluff products and systems· Proficiency in Microsoft Office and virtual meeting platforms· Ability and willingness to relocate twice:· First, to Florence, KY / Cincinnati, OH area for training· Then, to your assigned sales territory upon program completionBalluff is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. Fri, 10 Jul 2026 14:00:40 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11196883/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11288164 MCAC Adviser at University of Michigan Employer: University of Michigan \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n Job SummaryThe Center for Educational Outreach is seeking College Advisers to work with students and families across Michigan. If you are passionate about a commitment to equal access to education and believe in the power of community, we want to hear from you. We are specifically looking for recent graduates for this role. The College Adviser will be based at one of the following schools:Flint Southwestern Classical Academy, FlintPershing High School, DetroitPontiac High School, PontiacRiver Rouge High School, River RougeThis program aims to inspire students to explore higher education opportunities, guide them through university admissions and financial aid processes, and support them as they approach graduation. Advisers are required to live near their assigned school and expected to be present on-site at the designated high school during regular school hours (40 hours a week).This position will run from August 2026 to June 30, 2027. There will be mandatory summer training in Ann Arbor during the month of August. If you start after training has already begun, we are able to get you caught up on any training you may have missed and make sure you have everything you need to be successful in the role. Upon completion of the first year, advisers may have the option to extend their commitment for one additional school year, subject to the discretion of the Michigan College Access Corps (MCAC) program.Responsibilities*Help students complete and submit admissions and financial aid applications (FAFSA).Develop a comprehensive college timeline for each student, including application deadlines for admissions and financial aid.Assist students in interpreting correspondence from colleges, including offers of admission and financial aid.Provide information about high school course selection, test-taking skills, and basic financial planning to prepare students for future education.Organize group events that encourage students and their families to consider, plan for, and apply to colleges and universities.Work with local community groups and non-profits to offer events outside the school setting and hours.Host regular workshops for families to discuss topics such as financial aid, the college planning timeline, the importance of post-secondary education, and other opportunities.Establish productive working relationships with principals, counselors, and teachers in the assigned high school.Assist the program director and evaluation staff to collect and interpret progress and outcome data to evaluate the effectiveness of the MCAC program.Collaborate with the MCAC program director and school personnel to assess school needs and adapt programs and activities to meet these needs.Seek advice and counsel from the on-site supervisor at the assigned high school to support the long-term sustainability of the program.Participate in weekly staff meetings and professional development sessions throughout the year.Required Qualifications*A Bachelor's degreeAbility to pass federal and state background screenings.Strong planning and organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects.Experience in manipulating or analyzing data.Creativity and initiative in developing new programs.Desired Qualifications*A Bachelor's degree with a graduation date no earlier than May 2024.Prior experience in program 