n and manufacturing activitiesAssist with engineering and reporting tasksFollow company safety and quality proceduresParticipate in continuous improvement projectsComplete assigned development milestonesWork with mentors, supervisors, and engineers throughout the programPreferred QualificationsRecent Associate Degree graduates in:CNC Machining TechnologyMechanical Engineering TechnologyManufacturing TechnologyIndustrial TechnologyMechatronicsRelated technical programsPreferred skills include mechanical aptitude, basic computer skills, strong attendance, willingness to learn, and ability to work in a team environment.What We OfferStructured technical development programHands-on manufacturing and engineering experienceMentorship from experienced professionalsCareer growth opportunitiesExposure to advanced manufacturing operationsLeadership and technical skill developmentPhysical RequirementsAbility to work in a manufacturing environmentAbility to stand and move throughout the facilityAbility to safely use PPE and follow safety proceduresEqual Opportunity EmployerSundaram Clayton is an equal opportunity employer committed to creating an inclusive workplace for all employees. Additional InformationThis position is based onsite at Sundaram Clayton USA, LLC.Relocation assistance is not available for this program.Visa sponsorship or employment sponsorship is not available.This program is intended for recent graduates seeking entry-level manufacturing and engineering development opportunities. Mon, 10 Aug 2026 15:19:47 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11288925/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11116703 Trainee/Account Executive - Process /Plant Engineering at Neilsoft Inc. Employer: Neilsoft Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n  Title: Trainee/Account Executive - Process /Plant EngineeringLocation: Canton, MichiganExperience: 0–2 Years Neilsoft is a 1550+ people, technology-driven, Engineering Services and Solutions company servicing international customers for over 25+ years in the Architecture, Engineering and Construction (AEC), Manufacturing and Industrial Plant segments. We are headquartered in Pune (India) with international offices in US, Canada, UK, Germany and Japan. Neilsoft Inc. (a wholly owned subsidiary of Neilsoft Limited) has been supporting North American customers for more than two decades.  As part of our Growth Plans, we are looking to onboard 0-2 years experienced engineering graduates who aspire to build a career in Sales.  After completing structured training, candidates will be assigned to different industry verticals based on their strengths, interests, and performance, ensuring a strong foundation for long‑term career development.Neilsoft’s Process / Plant Engineering Practice offers multi-disciplinary plant engineering services, plant digitization  (intelligent P&IDs, Scan-to-3D) and Digital twin solutions for Owner/Operators, EPCs / Engineering Consultants and Fabricators. We cater to customer projects in several industries including Chemical, Oil & Gas / Energy, Food & Beverages, Renewables, Alternate Energy, Biofuels, BESS, Recycling and Clean technologies. To know more about the company please visit www.neilsoft.com  Responsibilities:Assist in identifying target accounts, generating leads, and building a qualified prospect funnel.Support business development activities for defined industry verticals and offerings Participate in client interactions, meetings, and presentations alongside senior team members.Learn the complete sales cycle—from prospecting to closure—under the mentorship of a Senior Sales professional.Create a plan to address defined markets & execute on the plan to achieve business/revenue targets Ideal Candidates will have:0-2 years experience, Bachelor’s degree in Chemical, Mechanical, Electrical Engineering (preferred).MBA or business coursework is mandatory.Passionate to build a career in Sales Strong communication skills, curiosity, and willingness to engage with clientsSelf