ampus involvement is a plus, but not requiredWhat You'll GainPaid training and ongoing mentorshipProfessional development in sales, marketing, and account managementLeadership and advancement opportunities based on performanceExperience working with nationally recognized brandsA collaborative and team-focused work environmentScheduleFull-TimeThursday–Monday10:00 AM–7:00 PMCompensationProjected weekly earnings: $1,000–$1,500Performance-based compensation structureIdeal for students seeking full-time opportunities and individuals looking to start a career in sales, business development, marketing, or customer relations. Thu, 11 Jun 2026 14:58:43 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11120048/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11121336 Medical Assistant at Medovate Dermatology Employer: Medovate Dermatology \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n If you are graduating and looking for meaningful experience, Medovate Dermatology is hiring! This opportunity is ideal for students in their gap years, and many of our former medical assistants have successfully gone on to medical and physician assistant school. No certification is required—just a strong willingness to learn and grow! Catalysts are expected to perform their duties in accordance with the Medovate Oath(e.g. to have an ownership attitude by being an ambassador/representative of our mission, vision, values, culture, and philosophy.   Please submit your resume to this link, and one of our hiring leads will reach out to you via email for an interview and job application! We are not currently considering applicants that are still in undergrad, as this is a full time position. We encourage you to apply once you have graduated, or when our summer intern programs open up. Thu, 11 Jun 2026 19:02:08 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11121336/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10491221 Behavior Therapist - ABA (Applied Behavior Analysis) Clinic at The Bridge Autism Clinic Employer: The Bridge Autism Clinic \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n  **** Next available start dates between October-December****  Thank you for your interest in The Bridge Autism Clinic! The Bridge Autism Clinic is currently seeking eager and enthusiastic undergrads or post graduate students who are looking for an opportunity to broaden their knowledge within the field of Psychology while getting hands-on experience working with children with autism. Get practical experience and learn more about the discipline of Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA).After your training period, you will assist our Behavior Therapists in providing 1:1 Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) therapy to children (ages 2-10) with Autism Spectrum Disorder (ASD). We are looking for passionate and professional candidates who appreciate how ABA therapy can help facilitate independence and enhance the quality of life for children with Autism.We offer a supportive, team-oriented environment grounded in best practices in ABA therapy. You will work under the direct supervision of our clinical leadership team, which includes BCBAs and credentialed Directors in ABA, Speech-Language Pathology, and Occupational Therapy.Requirements: Completed bachelor’s degree preferred or currently enrolled in school to obtain a bachelor’s degree of a similar or related field. ex: (Psychology, Special Education, Education, Social Work, Nursing, Counseling, Neuroscience/ Cognitive Science, Child and Adolescent Development)Experience working with children with developmental disorders or childcare in a professional environment is preferred.Must have a willingness to work with children ages 2-11 years of age. Available to work a 40-hour weekPossess strong organizational skills and attention to detailExercises good judgment at all timesAbility to communicate professionally and discretelyCreative and FlexibleSelf-Motivated and EnergeticUses social media responsiblyAdheres to HIPAA Rules and RegulationsValid Driver's LicenseBenefits:Competitive pay ($18-$21 per hour)Medical/Dental/Vision Insurance (full-time employment only)401K Plan with an up to 4% matchingFSA Paid Time Off/ Sick Time Referral programRegistered Behavior Technician (RBT) CredentialingOpportunities to advance within our professional career trackOngoing Training and Mentoring Mon, 10 Nov 2025 14:30:24 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/10491221/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11121363 Entitlements Coordinator at D.R. Horton, Inc. Employer: D.R. Horton, Inc. \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n D.R. Horton, Inc., the largest homebuilder in the U.S., was founded in 1978 and is a publicly traded company on the New York Stock Exchange. It is engaged in the construction and sale of high quality homes designed principally for the entry-level and first time move-up markets. The Company also provides mortgage financing and title services for homebuyers through its mortgage and title subsidiaries. Please visit our website at www.drhorton.com for more information.D.R. Horton, Inc. is currently looking for an Entitlements Coordinator in Operations Department. The right candidate will perform various accounting or finance functions with limited supervision by being able to identify issues, research, develop solutions and implement such solutions. Essential Duties and Responsibilities include the following. Other duties may be assigned.Participate in the entire due diligence process, including the physical and financial feasibility of a planned communityAid in the coordination of legal counsel or consultants, the review/revision of plans, the acquisition of city or county approvalMonitor and coordinate all other public hearings, including variances, amendments, etc.Attend meetings with city staff, the development team, as well as public hearings or neighbor meetingsMonitor the completion, submittal, and approval of construction plans, including soliciting bids for engineers and other consultants, coordinating the submittal of construction plans, zone and plat projectsConduct research of comps in the area. Prepare applications and submit appeals to the county, and attend the tax appeal hearingsReview Impact fee audit agreements, development and school agreements, etc.Conduct all business in a professional and ethical manner to serve customers and increase the goodwill and profit of the company QualificationsEducation and/or ExperienceBachelor’s degree from four-year college or universityOne to three years of related experience and/or trainingProficiency with MS Office and email Preferred QualificationsStrong communication skillsAbility to multi-task and attention to detail Salary: $90,000 - $110,000 annually Come join a winning team with a Fortune 500 company! We are growing fast and are looking for enthusiastic attitudes and team players to join our success. We offer an excellent benefits package including:Medical, Dental and Vision401(K)Employee Stock Purchase PlanFlex Spending AccountsLife & Disability InsuranceVacation, Sick, Personal Time and Company HolidaysMultiple Voluntary and Company provided Benefits Build YOUR future with D.R. Horton, America’s Builder. #WeBuildPeopleToo Thu, 11 Jun 2026 19:23:09 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11121363/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11289365 Project / Field Manager at Miller Integrated Solutions Employer: Miller Integrated Solutions \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n Project / Field Manager (Environmental Management Systems)Employment Type: Full-TimeTarget Majors: Environmental Management Systems, Geology, Biology, Natural Resource ManagementMinimum GPA: 2.75 About the RoleWe are seeking motivated students or recent graduates from programs in Environmental Management Systems (EMS), Geology, Natural Resource Management, Biology, or related environmental and life‑science fields. This position is ideal for individuals interested in applied environmental fieldwork, compliance activities, and industrial environmental management. All technical skills will be taught on the job, making this an excellent opportunity for those looking to gain hands‑on experience in the environmental sector.This role includes annual performance reviews and requires candidates to complete a pre‑employment physical, drug screen, and MVR evaluation. Job TitleProject / Field Manager Responsibilities(All skills will be trained on-the-job)Water discharge permit compliance sampling; DMR preparation and submittalsQuarterly monitor well sampling and LDEQ report preparationSoil sampling using a Geoprobe™ and/or manual hand augerLaboratory bottle preparation and chain-of-custody documentationHazardous, nonhazardous, and E&P waste management, including:Waste profiling and profile samplingLabeling and documentationLogistics coordinationRefinery safety training and periodic refinery site visitsObtain and maintain TWIC certification QualificationsPursuing or holding a B.S. in Environmental Management Systems, Geology, Natural Resource Management, Biology, or a related environmental or life‑science fieldMinimum GPA: 2.75Valid driver’s license; ability to pass MVR screeningAbility to meet physical and safety requirements for fieldworkRelevant environmental experience (private or government) is not required, but considered a plus Application InstructionsApplicants upload:Résumé Any relevant experience related to environmental fieldwork, compliance, sampling, waste management, or similar rolesExperience is not required but will be considered favorably. CompensationSalary or hourly pay will be discussed upon offer. Mon, 10 Aug 2026 16:23:52 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11289365/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10280545 Middle School Language Arts Teachers at Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) Employer: Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) \n\n Expires: 09/10/2026 \n\n Qualifications:Professional Educator License (PEL) issued by the Illinois State Board of Education (ISBE) Learning Objectives:Developing and maintaining IEPs , assessing student learning, adapting cu