 customer into our organization and engineering teams. Lead pricing discussions with the global sales networkSet pricing in conjunction with divisional objectives for sales and operating profit – gain Industry Manager, Industry Director, and Sales VP approval.Visit customers to promote new technology, support our sales channel or gain industry and application knowledgeCoordinate visits to Marshalltown including technical training and industry schoolsCollaborate with sales engineers, product engineers and marketing managersReview commercial terms and conditions for contracts and align on acceptable business risks – gain alignment from Industry Manager and Industry Director.Expedite and advance key customer complaints in focused industry segment and problems as is required to acquire satisfactory and timely resolution.Understand the complete Fisher portfolio for solutions and technologies, including new products, critical service valves, and FIELDVUE instrumentation. Who You Are:You quickly take actions in fact-changing, unexpected situations. Establish common objectives and a shared mentality. Enjoy dynamic working environments and team collaboration. Comfortable promoting your technical background to provide solutions. Adjust communication content and style to meet the needs of diverse collaborators.  For This Role, You Will Need:BS in Engineering, or qualified technical 4-year degree and combined experienceExperience working on teamsStrong communication skillsBusiness insightOpen to travelLegal authorization to work in the United States - Sponsorship will not be provided for this position. Preferred Qualifications That Set You Apart:Knowledge of control valves and/or process controlStrong presentation skills Thu, 23 Jul 2026 18:42:40 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11235358/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10280423 High School Science Teachers at Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) Employer: Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) \n\n Expires: 09