le for designing and publishing social media advertisement following compliance guidelines.  Must provide exceptional customer service while following policies and procedures. Must have computer skills and excellent communication skills.   Must always dress professionally.    Specific Duties but not limited to: Plans, develops, and directs the strategic and tactical marketing plans for the bank. Ensure that marketing objectives and plans support the overall business goals and objectives.Develop and implement policies and activities such as market research, advertising and promotion, and new product development.Responsible for developing and implementing the bank’s marketing plan and strategies to meet changing competitive conditions and products includes duties associated with marketing, communication, and advertising. Handle the coordination and administrative support for marketing activities in advertising, promotion, and community events.Designs, develops, and manages implementation of written and graphical content for websites and all social media platforms to provide information on products and services. Must attend public events representing the Bank during and after banking hours with the ability to manage and direct other bank employees to attend the event(s). Responsible for Ad designs for all advertisement which includes but not limited to Social Media, Radio, Billboard, Television, and Signage.Ability to pull Google/Search Engine Optimization reports to demonstrate the bank website performance.Maintain accurate spreadsheet records of all marketing requests and maintain budget for market expenses.Research marketing and promotional items, documenting pricing and order history, and staying informed of trends.Maintain a professional working relationship with all points of contact requesting sponsorships or donations, local business owners, customers, and bank employees.Notify appropriate persons requesting marketing donations. Performs special projects, and additional duties and responsibilities as required. Prepare weekly marketing information to present in COOC (Chief Operations Officers Committee) meetings. Must be able to perform multiple daily tasks and work under pressure with speed and accuracy.Must be available to work at least 40+ hours/ week Requirements:            Minimum of 2 years college education experienceDegree and experience in marketing and public relations, preferredMarketing Project Management Experience, preferredSolid Computer Skills, minimum of 3 years of Microsoft OfficeMust be highly creative in designing social media platforms, radio scripts, digital signs, and have the ability to create and implement marketing campaignsKnowledge of Marketing TechniquesStrong Communication and Interpersonal SkillsFlexible to attend community events/functions outside of normal work hours including weekends as requiredMust have the ability to design using Canva Pro and be trained on InLighten Studio Pro and Ignite Digital Sign software.Willingness and aptitude to learn the various areas of the bank Tue, 11 Aug 2026 14:07:45 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11292948/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11295180 Sous Chef at Arbor Day Foundation Employer: Arbor Day Foundation \n\n Expires: 09/11/2026 \n\n Are you a force for good? Do you dream of sharing your experience in the culinary industry, leading a team, and being able to voice and implement your creative ideas? Does the opportunity to devote your talents to a cause much greater than yourself excite you? Arbor Day Foundation is a place you can do work that matters, with people who care, in an inspiring environment. As we say at the Foundation: life is short, love where you work.Arbor Day Farm is a property owned and operated by the Arbor Day Foundation. This property is where our missions come to life! As one of the world's largest operating conservation foundations, the Arbor Day Foundation educates and engages stakeholders and communities across the globe to involve themselves in its mission of planting, nurturing, and celebrating trees. Our vision is to help others understand and use trees as a solution to many of the global issues we face today, including air quality, water quality, climate change, deforestation, poverty, and hunger.We need a Sous Chef to create and develop!You Have:Leadership skills. A proven ability to select, train, support, and develop supervisors and front-line staffPositive energy. A hands-on team player with a proven track record of translating ideas into effective action.Experience and passion. When it comes to cooking methods, kitchen equipment, best practices, and 1+ years of experience in a related role.Outstanding communication skills. Whether it be written or verbal, this comes naturally to you.Technology aptitude. You have a broad and in-depth understanding of MS- Word, and other restaurant related software programs.You Will:Develop and create. New menu options based on seasonal changes and customer demand. Assisting with the preparation and planning of meal designsSupervise. Establish training plans, engage team members, performance evaluation, scheduling, staffing, and inventoryImplement. Always adhering to safety and sanitation regulations, training new team members in these areasManage. In the Executive Chef’s absence, you are running the kitchen and managing the staff with strong leadership and communication skillsProvide Support. To junior kitchen employees with various tasks, including line cooking, food preparation, and dish platingLove Where You Work:We’re in this together. A culture focused on kindness, collaboration, and the intrinsic shared purpose to do what’s right. We pride ourselves on the culture we’ve built. We love it, and we know you will too.We care about your health. Competitive healthcare (health, dental, vision) coverage for you and your loved ones matched with a wellness incentives program.We invest in your future. Company paid short-term and long-term disability, life insurance, and 401k with company match.We want to stay connected. We’ll include you on our property-wide communications so you can stay in the know of company initiatives.We care about your mental health. We offer an EAP (Employee Assistance Program) where you and your family can access free counseling sessions and much more support.We’ll round out the experience. We put our culture first, and we host events and experiences throughout the year to show that we care about you (and your family). Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:10:39 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11295180/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11295199 Assistant Restaurant Manager at Arbor Day Foundation Employer: Arbor Day Foundation \n\n Expires: 09/11/2026 \n\n Does the opportunity to devote your talents to a cause much greater than yourself excite you? At Arbor Day Farm, you don’t just show up to work — you help create experiences rooted in purpose, service, and impact. Life is short, love where you work.  As one of the world’s largest conservation organizations, the Arbor Day Foundation inspires people to plant, nurture, and celebrate trees. Through Arbor Day Farm, Lied Lodge, Tree Adventure, and our historic properties, we bring that mission to life — welcoming guests to experience conservation firsthand.  Join Arbor Day Farm as an Assistant Restaurant Manager and help create meaningful guest experiences while advancing the Foundation’s mission right here in Nebraska City. Your Support System:You’ll report to our Restaurant Manager. You’ll collaborate with leaders and team members across the property, including Culinary. We believe in servant leadership, open communication, and growing talent from within. How We Work: Location: Nebraska City, Nebraska – Arbor Day Farm Campus Schedule: Full-Time; requires availability to work a variety of shifts, including mornings, evenings, weekends, holidays, and special events. Regular leadership coverage is expected during peak service periods, including weekend brunches and evening dining service. Our campus is guest-centered and hospitality-driven. Many roles require flexibility to support weddings, conferences, seasonal festivals, and signature events. We work hard, support each other, and believe if we’re going to do something — it’s worth doing well. What You’ll Do:Lead. Guide, mentor, coach, and assist Team Members in restaurant and lounge operations to ensure they feel supported and have the tools they need to perform at a high level.Be present on the floor. Maintain a visible leadership presence during service, coaching Team Members in real time, supporting service standards, and helping create exceptional guest experiences.Engage with guests. From the moment they arrive and throughout their visit, you'll help ensure guests feel welcomed, valued, and cared for while resolving concerns and creating memorable experiences.Support daily operations. Assist with scheduling, staffing, opening and closing responsibilities, beverage ordering and inventory management, and other operational needs that keep the restaurant running smoothly.Partner with Culinary. Work closely with the kitchen team to ensure communication, coordination, and execution are seamless between front- and back-of-house operations.Lead during peak business periods. Provide leadership coverage during evenings, weekends, holidays, special events, and seasonal high-volume periods.Model our Core Values. Your performance and behavior will align with our core values.What You’ll Bring:2+ years of restaurant, hospitality, or food and beverage leadership experience.Experience in a bar, lounge, or bartending environment required.Ability to lead in a fast-paced restaurant environment while balancing guest experience, team development, and operational execution.Strong understanding of front-of-house operations and the ability to communicate effectively with both front- and back-of-house teams.Passion for hospitality, service, and the Foundation's mission.Team-first mindset.Strong communication and coaching skills.Ability to adapt in a fast-paced environment.Eagerness to learn and grow.Commitment to high standards — because good enough is not good enough.What Success Looks Like:Guests consistently receive exceptional service and leave feeling welcomed, valued, and cared for.Service standards are visible, maintained, and consistently executed throughout the restaurant and loungeTeam Members are engaged, supported, coached, and held accountable to expectations.Restaurant operations run efficiently during peak periods, including evenings, weekends, holidays, and special events.You contribute to a culture rooted in kindness, collaboration, accountability, and excellence.Love Where You Work: Benefits & Perks: We’re in this together. A culture focused on kindness, collaboration, and doing what’s right.We care about your health. Competitive healthcare (medical, dental, vision) coverage paired with wellness incentives.We invest in your future. Company-paid short-term and long-term disability, life insurance, and 401(k) with company match.We care about your mental health. Access to an Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for you and your family.We will feed you. One complimentary meal per day.We’ll round out the experience. Property-wide events and experiences throughout the year. Exclusive perks. Free access to Tree Adventure, discounts on overnight stays, retail, and dining at Timbers and Porters, golf, and more.Full-Time and Part-Time Team Members are eligible for paid time off, including vacation, sick leave, floating holiday, and end-of-year floating holiday hours. Peak Team Members earn sick leave in accordance with Nebraska's Paid Sick Leave law.How to Apply: We’re excited you’re considering growing your career with us at Arbor Day Farm.  After you apply, we aim to follow up within one to two weeks via email from Paycom with the next steps.   Our hiring process typically includes: A phone conversation with our Recruiter or People TeamAn in-person interview with the hiring managerAdditional conversations depending on the role  The Arbor Day Foundation is an equal opportunity employer.    The Arbor Day Foundation is committed to equal employment opportunities. We will not discriminate against Team Members or applicants for employment on any legally recognized basis [“protected class”] including, but not limited to: veteran status, uniform servicemember status, race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, marital status, national origin, age, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, physical or mental disability, genetic information or any other protected class under federal, state, or local law.     We participate in E-Verify and will provide the federal government with your Form I-9 information to confirm your authorization to work in the U.S.   If you need reasonable accommodation to complete your application or participate in the interview process, please contact us at 402-873-8733. Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:12:22 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11295199/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10283129 High School Health Education Teachers at Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) Employer: Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) \n\n Expires: 09/11/2026 \n\n Learning Objectives:Developing and maintaining IEPs , assessing student learning, adapting curriculum, collaborating with other educators and encouraging students.  TEACHING PROCEDURESDifferent types of instructional techniques are used within the classroom.Demonstrates the ability to focus on and utilize current events in learning situations.Varies motivational techniques to hold pupil’s attention in the classroom.Display skill in questioning to elicit appropriate student response.Makes effective use of required and supplemental instructional materials.Uses positive reinforcement to encourage learning on the part of students.Introduces lessons effectively.Conducts summaries and reviews in an eff