te the cost of college.Today, we're building on that foundation by combining high-quality content, dependable scholarship data, modern search strategy, and AI-assisted workflows to better serve students and families.About the RoleWe're looking for a curious, detail-oriented Content Strategist & Writer who loves researching, writing, asking good questions, and turning complex information into content people can actually understand and use.This role combines four primary areas:Content Creation | Research | SEO & Search | Scholarship DataYou'll help create and improve the content students and families rely on, research topics related to scholarships and higher education, optimize content for how people search today, and help ensure the scholarship information on Scholarships.com is accurate and current.Exceptional recent graduates are encouraged to apply.What You'll DoResearch, write, edit, and update articles, guides, scholarship resources, and other student- and parent-facing content.Research scholarship, financial aid, college, and education-related topics and turn complex information into clear, accurate, and engaging content.Develop ideas for new content based on student needs, search behavior, emerging topics, and opportunities to improve Scholarships.com.Apply SEO best practices, including search intent, keyword research, headings, internal linking, page structure, and content freshness.Help optimize content for both traditional search engines and emerging AI-powered search and answer platforms.Review and improve existing content to keep it accurate, relevant, useful, and competitive in search results.Review scholarship listings for accuracy, completeness, eligibility requirements, deadlines, award amounts, and clear descriptions.Research and verify scholarship information using credible sources and reconcile conflicting information when necessary.Identify ways to improve how scholarship information and other content are organized and presented to students.Use tools such as ChatGPT and Claude to assist with research, content development, ideation, and quality checks—while independently verifying information and applying human judgment before anything is published.Collaborate with our content, product, and engineering teams to continually improve Scholarships.com.Who We're Looking ForWe're especially interested in candidates from research- and writing-intensive academic backgrounds, including:History | English | Journalism | Communications | Political Science | Philosophy | Sociology | Education | MarketingYou may be a great fit if you:Have a bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university.Are an exceptional recent graduate or have relevant experience through internships, employment, research, publications, campus organizations, or similar work.Have excellent research and source-analysis skills.Can determine whether information is trustworthy and verify facts before publishing.Are a strong writer, editor, and proofreader.Can make complicated information clear and concise.Are intellectually curious and highly attentive to detail.Are interested in SEO, search behavior, and how people discover information online.Are interested in scholarships, higher education, financial aid, or helping students navigate the college process.Are comfortable using AI tools while understanding when information needs to be independently researched and verified.Are comfortable learning CMS platforms, spreadsheets, analytics tools, and other digital technologies.What You'll GainThis is an opportunity to build practical experience across content strategy, professional writing, SEO, research, AI-assisted workflows, and scholarship-data curation while contributing to a platform used by students and families nationwide.You'll work directly with experienced team members across content, product, and engineering and have opportunities to take on greater responsibility as you grow.Position DetailsLocation: 513 Central Avenue, Suite 300, Highland Park, IL 60035Work Arrangement: Full-Time, On-Site OnlySchedule: Monday–Friday, 8:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m. CT, with a one-hour lunch breakSalary: $50,000–$60,000, depending on experience and qualificationsOur office is conveniently located near the Highland Park Metra station.BenefitsBlue Cross / Blue Shield PPO health insurance401(k)15 days of Paid Time Off7 paid holidaysCasual, collaborative office environmentOpportunities for professional growth and increased responsibilityHow to ApplyPlease submit:Your resumeA brief cover letter explaining how your academic background, research experience, and writing skills have prepared you for this roleRecent graduates are encouraged to apply. Tue, 11 Aug 2026 19:37:15 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11295478/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11046339 School Social Worker at Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) Employer: Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) \n\n Expires: 09/11/2026 \n\n QUALIFICATIONS:A. Master’s Degree in Social Work B. Type 73 Certificate Learning Objectives:A. Excellent clinical skills including assessment, counseling, etc. B. Excellent interpersonal skills C. Excellent written and oral communication skills D. Knowledge of resources within the school system and the community E. Knowledge of testing and evaluation processes within the school setting REPORTS TO:The school social worker is responsible to the Director of Special EducationSUPERVISES:N/AJOB GOAL:Exercise a high degree of initiative and professional judgment in providing schoolsocial worker services while working within the established framework of the federal        and state regulations and local school district policies. PERFORMANCE RESPONSIBILITIES:A. Participate in data analysis, including MTSS and case study evaluation     processesB. Conduct Social Developmental Studies and serve on IEP teamsC. Serve as Secondary PBIS CoachD. Write reports and maintain recordsE. Provide direct services to individual students and student groupsF