derstood and met, while providing exceptional servicePresent results to customers and internal teamsForecast facility and equipment needs in partnership with internal teams and other MGA locations Requirements & Skills: Bachelor of Engineering degree or related technical fieldValid driver’s license with a clean driving recordAuthorized to work in the United StatesAbility to manage and advance multiple projects simultaneously Keen attention to detail, coupled with a strong ability to identify errorsAbility to travel occasionally as part of onboarding, professional development, and customer meetings  Ideal Candidate: Ability to thrive in a dynamic and constantly changing environment Ability to be proactive and seek out opportunitiesAbility to act independently and make calculated decisions Desire to contribute to MGA’s business growth Familiarity with general automotive parts and components Benefits: Health & Dental InsurancePaid Sick/Vacation/HolidaysYearly discretionary bonuses, raises, profit sharing, and 401k matchingTuition reimbursement while employed at MGATravel opportunities between MGA and customer sitesOpportunities for career development and advancement Please visit our website for more information at https://www.mgaresearch.com/.MGA Research Corporation is an equal opportunity/affirmative action employer. Tue, 11 Aug 2026 21:22:40 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11296253/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/10283017 General Education PreK Teachers at Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) Employer: Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) \n\n Expires: 09/11/2026 \n\n Qualifications:Professional Educator License (PEL) issued by the Illinois State Board of Education (ISBE) Learning Objectives:Developing and maintaining IEPs , assessing student learning, adapting curriculum, collaborating with other educators and encouraging students.  TEACHING PROCEDURESDifferent types of instructional techniques are used within the classroom.Demonstrates the abi