ts other than SSI (ie: rating scale from a doctor’s office), copy forms                          completed by staff      6. Compile information for responseF. Special Education Department Clerical Support1. Sort and distribute all mail daily2. Type letters / memos as requested3. Send correspondence as requested4. Maintain and update sign-out board for all staff5. File documentation into student files6. Phone calls as requested7. Copying as requested8. Creating binders, materials for professional development, etc.) as requested9. Assist with registration of students as needed10. Assist with the distribution of materials to classrooms / teachers11. Assist with processing of supplies as neededG. Assist with organizing and maintaining suppliesH. Assist with maintenance of Department documentation (TOV, CPDU, Meetings,            CPI, WalMart PO)I. Any other duties and/or responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Special              Education or designee Wed, 13 May 2026 20:55:23 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11046942/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11124487 Special Education Department Staff Accountant at Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) Employer: Cahokia Unit School District #187 (IL) \n\n Expires: 09/11/2026 \n\n QUALIFICATIONS:A. Bachelor’s Degree in Accounting B. Skilled in the operation of standard office machinery C. Proficient in computer skills including word processing, spread sheets, data bases, and the internet. Excellent skills specifically in the use of Microsoft Excel required.Learning Objectives:A. Good communication and customer service skills and the ability to promote a positive image of the Special Education Department and CUSD #187 B. Ability to maintain confidentialityC. Good organizational skills and the ability to set priorities and meet deadlines while working on multiple projects at a time D. Ability to take initiative with job responsibilitiesREPORTS TO:The Director of Special Education or his/her designeeSUPERVI