ality of work performed.You will identify, analyze, advise, consult and report on scientific, theoretical, and factual data, conditions, and problems.You will assess, resolve and predict the relationships and interactions of data and findings under varying conditions. Wed, 10 Sep 2025 22:26:44 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/10286514/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11176003 Data Center Technician at EZSVS USA Employer: EZSVS USA \n\n Expires: 09/11/2026 \n\n Date posted: June 9, 2026Pay: $50,000.00 - $60,000.00 per yearJob description:Full job descriptionWork in customer’s data center.Install and configure from data link layer to application layer of the whole network system in the data center.Daily monitor and maintain the network; Ensure the network availability so that the remote users can have stable access to the servers.Engage in site layout, network construction planning and quality control; Ensure data safety.Supervise server support specialist to diagnose, troubleshoot, and resolve hardware, software, or other network and system problems, and replace defective components when necessary.Skills and Qualifications:Knowledge of L1-L7 network architecture, TCP/IP, Switching, Routing, and Optical communication technologyExperience installing servers and their components including installing boards, cards, hard drives, and a diverse number of software products;Strong troubleshooting and communication skills to be able to analyze hardware and software problems; research and resolve complex issues; and interface with customers, manufacturers, and technical support staff;Ability to diagnose data communications problems with using specialized tools, test equipment, and software utilities;Experience interacting with both coworkers and customers;A+ and CCNA certifications; and/or training from applicable hardware and software manufacturers will be an asset;Knowing power and air flow system will be an asset;Job Type: Full-timeBenefits: 401(k) matchingDen