g team to ensure continued development, support, and goal alignmentRegularly communicate customer feedback, service trends, and insights with team leads to improve the sales campaign effectivenessContribute to a high-performing, energetic team culture by sharing successful sales techniques and supporting teammatesSubmit daily sales results and progress reports to the executive team to help measure performance and team goalsWhat We’re Looking For in an Entry Level Sales Associate:Driven individuals who take pride in problem-solving and building strong, lasting client relationshipsExcellent communicators who can confidently present ideas and listen actively to client needsTeam players who thrive in a collaborative, fast-paced environmentSelf-starters with a proactive mindset and a strong desire to grow professionallyDetail-oriented individuals who bring structure, organization, and follow-through to every projectPassionate about sales, customer experience, and making an impact from day onePrevious experience or education in sales, business, or communications is a plus—but not required Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:15:21 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11297462/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11299617 Fab Technician at Absolics Inc Employer: Absolics Inc \n\n Expires: 09/12/2026 \n\n Position: FAB TechnicianLocation: COVINGTON, GA JOB SUMMARYWe are seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Semiconductor FAB Technician to join our Production Department. The technician will support daily manufacturing operations in a cleanroom environment, ensuring the safe, efficient, and high-quality production of semiconductor wafers. Job Duties/Responsibilities:· Operate, monitor, and maintain FAB equipment (e.g., etching, deposition, lithography).· Load and unload wafers from production tools with precision and care.· Perform equipment start-up, shutdown, and troubleshooting procedures.· Conduct production inspection for first article of the lot and model change.· Inventory of daily usage of raw materials and tools at the production line (e.g., chemicals, film, singulation tools).· Take initial and containment actions and troubleshooting when the machines are down.· Control the recipe and teach the inspection area for inspection machines.· Follow standard operating procedures (SOPs) and cleanroom protocols.· Log production data, machine status, and process issues accurately.· Collaborate with engineers and other operators to meet production goals.· Cooperate with regular maintenance and calibration of equipment.· Maintain cleanliness and safety within the FAB environment. Qualifications:Bachelor’s degree in engineering and science or equivalent required.Experience in semiconductor or cleanroom environments is a plus.Basic mechanical or electrical skills.Ability to follow detailed instructions and standard operating procedures.Comfortable working in a cleanroom with full protective gear (gown, gloves, mask).Willingness to work shifts (day, night, or rotating as needed).Good communication and teamwork skills. Work Schedule:8 to 12-hour shiftsPossible weekend or rotating schedule based on production needs. Preferred Skills (Nice to Have):Knowledge of wafer handling and FAB processes.Experience with MES (Manufacturing Execution Systems) & EMS (Equipment Management Systems).Familiarity with SPC (Statistical Process Control). Rate:$26 - $34 an hour Wed, 12 Aug 2026 17:37:14 +0000 https://wheatonma.joinhandshake.com/jobs/11299617/share_preview gid://handshake/Job/11112475 Outside Sales Representative at Landreth Lighting Employer: Landreth Lighting \n\n Expires: 09/12/2026 \n\n Landreth, Incorporated is seeking an outside salesperson responsible for managing and developing profitable, long-term business relationships with local design firms.  Customer base consists of architectural/interior design firms and electrical engineers focusing on commercial projects.Responsibilities:Develop and manage long-term strategic business relationships with key